  "rationale": "R4 exposed two protocol/recovery defects around ISS RE resignation messages. Official ISS client source defines RE as a cardplay resignation that ends immediately only when the declarer resigns; defenders require both defenders to resign. The same reference implementation explicitly treats RE and LE as out-of-order moves that do not replace the expected turn. V2 had treated every RE as terminal and exactly-once reconciliation had treated an out-of-order RE arriving before the echo of an already-sent card as the replacement move. Both defects are fixed and regression-tested.",
